.\" demoreel(1). README.md is the full account; this page is the reference.
.\" ci.sh checks it names every option, subcommand and step demoreel accepts.
.TH DEMOREEL 1 "" "demoreel" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
demoreel \- record a GUI app on a private virtual display
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B demoreel record
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B demoreel shot
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B demoreel stop
.RI [ name ]
.br
.B demoreel check
.br
.B demoreel edit
.I script
.B \-o
.I film.mp4
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B demoreel trim
|
.B caption
|
.B join
|
.B card
.RI [ options ]
.B \-o
.I out.mp4
.RI [ input ...]
.br
.B demoreel motion
.I video
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B demoreel poster
.I video
.B \-t
.I seconds
.B \-o
.I picture
.br
.B demoreel
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B demoreel
starts a private virtual display, runs
.I command
on it, sizes the app's window to fill the frame, and records it.
Your real desktop is never in the picture, because the app never runs there.
When the run succeeds,
.B demoreel
prints the path of the finished file on standard output, and nothing else.
The app's own output goes to standard error, or to
.BR \-\-app\-log .
.PP
A video is an H.264 MP4 with no sound.
A recording that is one flat colour is refused, not returned.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B record
Record the app and write a video file.
.TP
.B shot
Take one picture of the app and write a PNG.
It waits for the app to draw, runs any
.B \-a
steps, saves the picture and closes the app.
It takes the options of
.B record
except
.BR \-d ,
.B \-r
and
.BR \-n .
.TP
.B stop
End a running recording early, wait until its video is finished and checked,
and print its path.
With no
.IR name ,
it stops the only recording running.
It works straight after launching the run, even before it has started
recording.
.TP
.B check
Report what each backend needs and whether it is installed, start a private
display to prove it works, and name the install command for anything missing.
It records nothing.
.PP
The finishing commands work on video files, not on an app.
They start no display and take no
.BR \-n .
.TP
.B edit
Make a film from a script of scenes, encoding the picture once.
See
.BR "EDIT SCRIPT" .
.TP
.B trim
Cut the start and the end off a video:
one clip, with
.B \-\-from
and
.BR \-\-to .
.TP
.B caption
Put text over part of a video:
one clip, with one or more
.BR \-\-text .
.TP
.B join
Put two or more videos end to end.
.TP
.B card
Make a clip from a picture, from text, or both.
.TP
.B motion
Report how often a video's picture changes and where it stands still.
It writes no file; its report goes to standard output.
.TP
.B poster
Save the frame on screen at
.B \-t
as a picture.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Where to write the file.
For
.B record
and
.B shot
the default is the current directory, named after the app and the time.
The finishing commands require it:
a video must end in
.BR .mp4 ,
a
.B poster
picture in
.B .png
or
.BR .jpg ,
and it may not be a file the command reads.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-duration " \fIseconds\fR"
How long to record, counted from when the scripted steps finish (default 30).
.B \-d 0
records until
.B demoreel stop
or until the app closes itself.
For
.BR card ,
how long the card lasts; required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " \fIW\fBx\fIH\fR"
The size of the picture (default 1600x1000).
For a video, both numbers must be even.
For
.BR edit ,
the default is the first clip's size.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-framerate " \fIfps\fR"
Frames per second (default 30).
.BR record ,
.B edit
and
.BR card .
For
.BR edit ,
the default is the first clip's rate.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " \fIname\fR"
A name for this run, so
.B demoreel stop
can find it (default
.BR default ).
Two runs with the same name cannot record at once; the second refuses.
.B record
only.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-action " \fIstep\fR"
A scripted step, run while the app is recorded.
Repeat it; the steps run in order.
See
.BR STEPS .
.TP
.BI \-\-app\-log " path"
Save the app's own output in
.IR path .
.TP
.BI \-\-settle " seconds"
Wait up to
.I seconds
for the app to draw something before recording, instead of filming its black
startup screen.
The default is 0 for
.B record
and 10 for
.BR shot .
.TP
.B \-\-gpu
For an app that needs the graphics card (OpenGL, Vulkan).
The default display,
.BR Xvfb ,
has no GPU, so such an app records black on it.
This records on a headless
.B cage
compositor instead.
It needs
.BR cage ,
.B Xwayland
and
.BR wlr\-randr ,
and
.B record \-\-gpu
also needs
.BR wf\-recorder .
.TP
.B \-\-cursor
Draw the mouse pointer.
Off by default.
Not available with
.BR "record \-\-gpu" .
.TP
.BI \-\-startup\-timeout " seconds"
How long to wait for the app's window (default 20).
.TP
.BI \-\-from " seconds" "\fR, \fP" \-\-to " seconds"
.BR trim :
the part to keep; the frame on screen at
.B \-\-to
is the last one kept.
.BR motion :
the part to look at.
.BR caption :
when the
.B \-\-text
before it shows.
.TP
.BI \-\-fade\-in " seconds" "\fR, \fP" \-\-fade\-out " seconds"
Start from black, or end on black.
.BR trim ,
.BR caption ,
.B join
and
.BR card .
.TP
.BI \-\-fade\-at " seconds"
.BR trim :
fade to black and back around this moment, keeping the length.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-fade\-length " seconds"
How long each half of a
.B \-\-fade\-at
takes (default 0.5).
.TP
.BI \-\-crossfade " seconds"
.BR join :
fade from each video into the next, where a plain cut would be.
The videos overlap for that long.
.TP
.BI \-\-text " words"
One line of text.
.BR caption :
repeatable, shown on a dark band at the bottom.
.BR card :
the card's title.
.TP
.BI \-\-text\-size " percent"
The text's height as a percentage of the frame's
(default 5 for
.BR caption ,
7 for
.BR card ).
Text too wide for the frame is refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-background " #RRGGBB"
.BR card :
the background colour (default #101418).
.TP
.BI \-\-like " video"
.BR card :
take the size and frame rate from this video.
.TP
.BI \-\-still " seconds"
.BR motion :
report a stretch with no change longer than this (default 1).
.TP
.B \-\-json
.BR motion :
print the report as one JSON object.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time " \fIseconds\fR"
.BR poster :
which moment to save; required.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.B "demoreel \-\-help"
and
.B "demoreel record \-\-help"
end with worked examples.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH STEPS
Each
.B \-a
takes one step, quoted as one word:
.TP
.BI "wait " seconds
Pause.
.TP
.BI "move " "x y"
Move the pointer.
.TP
.BR click " [\fIx y\fR]"
Click there, or where the pointer already is.
The pointer starts in the bottom-right corner.
.TP
.BI "type " text
Type
.IR text ,
exactly as written after
.B type
and one space.
.TP
.BI "key " name
Press a key, such as
.B Return
or
.BR ctrl+s .
.TP
.BI "hold " "key seconds"
Hold a key down.
It is let go however the step ends.
.PP
Anything on a command line can be read by other users of the machine, so do
not script typing a password on a shared one.
.SH EDIT SCRIPT
One scene a line, played in order.
A blank line, or a line starting with
.BR # ,
is ignored.
A line is split into words as a shell splits one.
Times are seconds; on a clip they count from the start of its own file.
.TP
.BI "clip " file
Play a video.
Then any of
.BI from " s"\fR,\fP
.BI to " s"\fR,\fP
.BI fade\-in " s"\fR,\fP
.BI fade\-out " s"\fR,\fP
.BI fade\-at " s"\fR,\fP
.BI fade\-length " s"
and
.BI crossfade " s"\fR.\fP
.TP
.BI "card " "seconds \fR[\fPpicture\fR]\fP"
Show a plain background, with a picture on it, or text, or both.
A .gif or an animated .png keeps playing.
Then any of
.BI background " #RRGGBB"\fR,\fP
.BR fade\-in ,
.B fade\-out
and
.BR crossfade .
.TP
.BI "text " "\(dqwords\(dq"
Put one line of text on the scene above.
Then any of
.BI from " s"\fR,\fP
.BI to " s"
and
.BI size " percent"\fR.\fP
.PP
The whole script is checked before anything is made, and an error names its
line.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The file was written and checked, and its path printed.
For
.BR check ,
the default backend can record.
.TP
.B 1
The run failed, and the message on standard error says why and what to do.
A failed run prints no path.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was not understood.
.SH FILES
Run files live in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/demoreel\-UID ,
or
.I /tmp/demoreel\-UID
when that variable is unset.
The directory must belong to you.
.TP
.IB name .lock
Held for the whole of a run, so two runs cannot share a name.
.TP
.IB name .json
What
.B demoreel stop
reads to find the run and learn how it ended.
It stays after the run.
.TP
.IB name .ffmpeg.log "\fR, \fP" name .display.log
The recorder's and the display's logs.
Kept when a run fails, removed when it succeeds.
.TP
.I shot\-*
A folder for one
.BR shot ,
removed when it succeeds and kept, and named, when it fails.
.TP
.I check\-*
A folder for
.BR check 's
test display, always removed.
.TP
.I edit\-*
A folder for the texts of one film, always removed.
.SH NOTES
.SS A Flatpak app
A Flatpak does not see the private display on its own.
Give its own command line three flags:
.PP
.RS
.nf
demoreel record \-o demo.mp4 \-\- \e
  flatpak run \-\-socket=x11 \-\-nosocket=wayland \e
  \-\-filesystem=/tmp/.X11\-unix org.example.App
.fi
.RE
.SS An app already running
A single-instance app that is already open on your desktop hands the new launch
to its running copy, which exits at once.
Close the running copy first.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
demoreel check
demoreel record \-o demo.mp4 \-d 20 \-\- kate
demoreel record \-o demo.mp4 \-d 20 \-\-cursor \e
  \-a \(aqwait 2\(aq \-a \(aqclick 400 300\(aq \-a \(aqtype hello\(aq \-\- kate
demoreel record \-o demo.mp4 \-d 0 \-n mydemo \-\- kate &
demoreel stop mydemo
demoreel record \-o cube.mp4 \-d 10 \-\-gpu \-\- vkcube
demoreel shot \-o menu.png \-a \(aqclick 40 12\(aq \-\- kate
demoreel motion demo.mp4
demoreel trim demo.mp4 \-o short.mp4 \-\-to 29.8
demoreel edit film.txt \-o film.mp4
demoreel poster film.mp4 \-t 14.9 \-o poster.jpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Xvfb (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR xdotool (1),
.BR cage (1)
.PP
README.md in the source repository covers why each part works as it does.
